note as DEP_diagram_46_platform_ops
  Connects to other modules via:
  directory.tenants, iam.users, common.files (artifacts.file_id),
  terminology.catalog_concepts (all *_concept_id). Health checks may target any
  service component; artifacts reference the tool that produced them.
end note

note as REC_DERIVED_diagram_46_platform_ops
  REC 3.3 — DERIVED / OPERATIONAL STATE
  deployments.is_current, health_incidents (opened from consecutive failing
  health_check_runs) and any run rollups are DERIVED; maintain via trigger or
  scheduled recompute and reconcile. health_check_runs is append-only (<<LOG>>);
  correct by inserting a new run, never UPDATE/DELETE. artifacts.is_immutable
  artifacts must never be overwritten once built (content_hash pins identity).
end note

note as HARDENING_diagram_46_platform_ops
  REC 3.4 — HARDENING / PHYSICAL CONSTRAINTS (enforce at DDL)
  - component_tools: UNIQUE(service_component_id, tool_id, usage_concept_id).
  - deployments: partial UNIQUE(service_component_id, environment_concept_id)
    WHERE is_current; CHECK finished_at >= started_at.
  - health_checks: CHECK timeout_ms < interval_seconds*1000 AND unhealthy_threshold >= 1.
  - health_check_runs: append-only; PARTITION BY recorded_at (monthly) + retention;
    index (health_check_id, recorded_at DESC).
  - artifacts: content-addressable; content_hash/storage_uri immutable when is_immutable;
    UNIQUE(artifact_ref).
end note

note as VALUE_SETS_diagram_46_platform_ops
  VALUE SETS (bind *_concept_id; do not hardcode)
  component_type->vs_component_type{api,worker,database,cache,gateway,frontend,job,external};
  criticality->vs_criticality{tier1,tier2,tier3};
  tool_type->vs_tool_type{language,framework,orm,database,cache,message_broker,ci_cd,iac,
    container_runtime,monitoring,testing,security};
  usage->vs_tool_usage{runtime,build,test,deploy,monitor};
  artifact_type->vs_artifact_type{container_image,npm_package,nuget_package,db_migration_bundle,
    orm_schema,plantuml_render,sbom,backup,report};
  environment->vs_environment{dev,staging,production,dr};
  strategy->vs_deploy_strategy{rolling,blue_green,canary,recreate};
  deploy status->vs_deploy_status{pending,in_progress,succeeded,failed,rolled_back};
  check_type->vs_health_check_type{liveness,readiness,startup,dependency,synthetic,smoke};
  target_kind->vs_health_target_kind{http,tcp,grpc,sql_query,command,queue_depth};
  run status->vs_health_run_status{pass,warn,fail,timeout,error};
  run_source->vs_run_source{scheduler,manual,probe,ci};
  severity->vs_severity{info,warning,minor,major,critical};
  incident status->vs_incident_status{open,acknowledged,mitigated,resolved};
  state->vs_lifecycle_state{active,inactive,deprecated,retired}.
end note

